**Container/logic to know:** `main()` in `C:\Users\mmazur\.claude\helpers\luna-statusline.cjs`, lines ~241–249. There's no Grid/StackPanel/div — it's a plain-text terminal renderer, so "layout" = the `LEFTW` gutter (a number of spaces) computed before the wordmark is appended to each row.

**What changed:**
```js
const artW = Math.max(...art.map((a) => stripAnsi(a).length));
const cols = process.stdout.columns || 120;
const LEFTW = Math.max(
  Math.max(...left.map((s) => stripAnsi(s).length)) + 3,
  cols - artW
);
```
Before, `LEFTW` was just `widest-left-line + 3`, so the wordmark sat immediately after the status text. Now it's `max(that, terminal-width − wordmark-width)`, so the wordmark hugs the terminal's actual right edge — same physical location as your desktop icons — and re-anchors automatically if you resize the window. It only falls back to the old tight spacing if the terminal is too narrow for a full right-edge placement.

Open a new prompt (or resize the pane) to see it re-render at the new position.

